  <running_head>INDEX</running_head>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="2">1. Quot generum sint curatores?</l>
    <l n="3">2. Moribus testamento curator dari potest.</l>
    <l n="4" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="5">1. Inviti non accipiunt curatorem.</l>
    <l n="6">2. Moribus accipiunt.</l>
    <l n="7">3. Ad litem accipiunt curatorem, etiam</l>
    <l n="8">inviti.</l>
    <l n="9">4. Moribus sine curatore in causa crimi-</l>
    <l n="10">nali subsistere possunt.</l>
    <l n="11" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="12">1. Furioso datur curator.</l>
    <l n="13">2. Etiam conjux conjugi.</l>
    <l n="14">3. Prodigus quis sit?</l>
    <l n="15">4. Moribus quid requiratur, ut quis</l>
    <l n="16">dicatur prodigus?</l>
    <l n="17">5. Jure posteriori nondum est</l>
    <l n="18">sublata cura legitima.</l>
    <l n="19" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="20">1. Mente captis, surdis, mutis, &amp;c.</l>
    <l n="21">datur curator.</l>
    <l n="22">2. Non tamen caecis.</l>
    <l n="23" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 5.</l>
    <l n="24">Quandoque impuberibus datur</l>
    <l n="25">curator?</l>
    <l n="26" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 6.</l>
    <l n="27">Quandoque datur actor.</l>
    <l n="28" type="heading" level="1" caput="24" para="true">LIBR. I. INSTIT. TIT. 24.</l>
    <l n="29" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De Satisdat. Tutor. vel Curat.</l>
    <l n="30" type="heading" level="2" para="true">In Princ.</l>
    <l n="31" para="true">1. NOnnulla antecedunt tutoris ad-</l>
    <l n="32">ministrationem.</l>
    <l n="33">2. Non omnes tutores satisdant.</l>
    <l n="34">3. Non illi qui dati ex inquisitione.</l>
    <l n="35" type="heading" level="2" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="36" para="true">1. Si plures sint tutores, unus</l>
    <l n="37">offerre</l>
    <l n="38" para="true">2. Secundum Kabbinos plurium fagra-</l>
    <l n="39">giis est applaudendum.</l>
    <l n="40" para="true">3. De moribus quid obtineat circa satis-</l>
    <l n="41">dationem, explicatur.</l>
    <l n="42" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="43" para="true">1. Finita tutela conveniuntur tutores.</l>
    <l n="44" para="true">2. Etiam ipsorum haeredes.</l>
    <l n="45" para="true">3. Et fidejussores, postulatores &amp;c.</l>
    <l n="46" para="true">4. Denique magistratus municipales &amp;</l>
    <l n="47">ministri.</l>
    <l n="48" para="true">§. 3.</l>
    <l n="49" para="true">
      <i>Qui tutores non satisfant, coërcentur.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="50" para="true">§. 4.</l>
    <l n="51" para="true">1. Majores magistratus non conveniun-</l>
    <l n="52">tur.</l>
    <l n="53" para="true">2. Moribus quorundam cessat actio subsi-</l>
    <l n="54">diaria.</l>
    <l n="55" type="heading" level="1" caput="25" para="true">LIBR. I. INSTIT. TIT. 25.</l>
    <l n="56" type="heading" level="2" para="true">De Excus. Tutor. vel Curat.</l>
    <l n="57" type="heading" level="2" para="true">In Princ.</l>
    <l n="58" para="true">1. QUidam tutores excusare se non possunt.</l>
    <l n="59" para="true">2. Tutela est munus publicum.</l>
    <l n="60" para="true">3. Moribus causas excusationum volunt</l>
    <l n="61">esse arbitrarias.</l>
    <l n="62" para="true">4. Numerus liberorum excusat.</l>
    <l n="63" para="true">5. Liberorum nomine quinam veniant?</l>
    <l n="64" para="true">6. Moribus quid obtineat?</l>
    <l n="65" para="true">§. 1.</l>
    <l n="66" para="true">1. Semestria quid sint?</l>
    <l n="67" para="true">2. Procurator fisci excusatur.</l>
    <l n="68" para="true">3. Moribus quid statuendum?</l>
    <l n="69" para="true">§. 2.</l>
    <l n="70" para="true">1. Absentia reipublicae causa excusat.</l>
    <l n="71" para="true">2. Etiam ea quae est necessaria vel injusta.</l>
    <l n="72" para="true">§. 3.</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The right column is cut off and blanked out, except for a few fragmentary lines at the top right ("poteft satisdationem.", and a partly visible line below it). The left column's first lines are italic and bold in places; the drop-cap N is treated as a letter joined to the word. Some words at the right edge of the left column are cut by the blanking and are not transcribed. The left part of the scan is blank white and is not transcribed. The first lines are cut at the top; the bottom faint line under the column is partly illegible and was not transcribed. Initial Q of "Quidam" is a large woodcut-style initial.</notes>
